{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'git status --short; git diff --stat; cat collab/1791304223243-compiler-engineer-ucf-d14-source.findings.md'","aggregated_output":" M docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md\n M src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc\n M src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc\n M src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export_test.cljc\n?? collab/1791194000000-architect-m-next-d-plan-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md\n?? collab/1791231000000-architect-d9-header-ruling.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md\n?? collab/1791240000000-architect-d10-lower-inputs-ruling.gpt-6-astra.findings.md\n?? collab/1791304223243-compiler-engineer-ucf-d14-source.findings.md\n?? collab/1791304223243-compiler-engineer-ucf-d14-source.prompt.md\n?? collab/1791320000000-architect-d14-seam-ruling-astra.gpt-6-astra.findings.md\n .../design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md |   35 +-\n src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc                   |  203 ++-\n src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc             | 1913 ++++++++++++++++++--\n src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export.cljc             |  218 ++-\n test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver_test.cljc            | 1272 ++++++++++++-\n test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export_test.cljc            |  326 ++++\n 6 files changed, 3700 insertions(+), 267 deletions(-)\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-10-06 22:30:18 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-07 05:30:18 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh (+0700)\nCoding-Agent: Codex\n\n# D14 — complete export recovery and source/exit progress journal\n\n## Disposition\n\nImplementation completed under the architect's seam ruling. This report replaces the previous BLOCKED audit and covers the inherited partial implementation plus this rebuild. The final focused driver, independent seam/handoff suites, full JVM fast lane, lint and formatting checks are green. This is implementation evidence, not an architect sign-off.\n\nThe inherited implementation correctly established source/exit phases, mint-before-prepare ordering, the fork decision, initial request brackets, completion/report/release helpers, D13 tenure/run-end machinery and a holder-cleanup recovery branch. Its projection persistence, original-machine recovery, retry bookkeeping and several fixtures were insufficient. Those parts were rebuilt rather than retained as the recovery foundation.\n\n## Changed files and scope\n\n- `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export.cljc:313`: canonical freeze, fenced rehydration, recursive retained records, validation and restarted-abort refusal.\n- `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc:1`: shared administrative restoration, stable cell identities, full dependency census and pre-attachment recovery inspection.\n- `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc:1`: source/exit journal, storage, retries, enrollment, tenure and restart reconstruction.\n- `test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export_test.cljc:1`: authentic closures/cells, aliases, children, exact bytes, validation and zero-IO recovery rows.\n- `test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver_test.cljc:1`: durable brackets, source/exit cuts, recovery, enrollment and genuine residual-2 fixtures; corrected inherited invalid phase/count assumptions.\n- `docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1786`: correct the plain-live-record promise; document recovery, environment separation, exit ordering and restart safety.\n- `collab/1791304223243-compiler-engineer-ucf-d14-source.findings.md:1`: this report.\n\nNo Jing, authority, kernel or journal-backend code changed. No commits, branches or other git writes were performed. The tracked diff stays within the ruling's widened scope; other collaboration inputs were only read.\n\n## Complete recovery seam\n\n`export/freeze [machine prepared-record]` returns canonical recovery bytes/address beside exact published body bytes/address. The separate object has its own `:yin.k/export-recovery` tag and format version 1. It directly embeds verified codec snapshots and retains the preparation header/enrolled set, descriptors, waits, issue stamps, prior gates, children and fresh-name state. The enrolled set never enters a published body.\n\nValues use the existing handoff value/cell codec, not opaque Jing Closure encoding or value stringification. Base64 transports encoded bytes only. Census includes halted results, nested module stores and install children before finalizing dependencies. When legacy version-0 bytes omit transitive module dependencies, recovery retains an additional complete codec snapshot without altering published version-0 bytes. Snapshot roots and existing dependencies must agree with the published body before attachment.\n\n`export/rehydrate-fenced` validates addresses, version, header, descriptors, dependencies and recursive metadata before administrative attachment. It restores authentic fresh-receiver-owned closures/references, preserves aliases and distinct cells, reinstalls carried FFI/link routes and reproduces exact published bytes. Root and children stay exporting, with waits/parks outside scheduler queues. Receiver guest bindings, closes and issue state cannot contaminate reconstruction. Child reconstruction disables native stream-pair creation and never executes initialization.\n\nCounting handles prove zero reads, cursor mints, writes, closes or guest execution during reconstruction. Recovered records cannot abort back into execution. Runnable public lower remains separate and grant-admitted. The object is self-contained; the optional fetch seam is unnecessary for this format. Runtime composition functions and live machines remain environment, not journal data.\n\nThe initial independent seam/handoff gate passed **64 tests / 659 assertions** before the journal/recovery rebuild. The final expanded independent gate passed **69 tests / 702 assertions**.\n\n## Whole-task contract audit\n\n| Contract | Completed behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1. Export / fork / prepare | Landed enter/prepare/encode retained, including alias-aware retained serving answers. Nil arbitration follows the unchanged version-0 fork without occurrence, offer or journal bracket. |\n| 2. Mint once before prepare | Source and successor/result occurrence/header are journaled before prepare. Serving and each content-store put have write-ahead intents and acknowledgments. Recovery and exact body are durable before the fenced event. |\n| 3. Brackets / stable proposals | Offer, proposal, report, release and renewal deliveries/retries have intent before send, attempt afterward and authenticated acknowledgment. Proposal replay retains its sent id; intent selection follows explicit journal order. Accepted grants are durable before lower attachment. |\n| 4. Abort / attempts | Every unmatched offer intent retains unknown delivery. A successful/uncertain retry cannot disappear after failed attempt append. Authority refusal is not non-delivery evidence. Holder abort uses successful renewal basis and authoritative tenure; recovered records never revive execution. |\n| 5. Exit / cuts / halt | Persist recovery/body, fence, attempt successor offer, report exact body, release matching origin lease, observe exact closure/edge, retry stable offer until admitted. Awaiting-completion does not block reporting. Halt reports result/terminal edge without successor offer. |\n| 6. Tenure through exit | Renewal retained, with checks before prepare, serve, storage and exit sends. Renewal carriage is journaled before application, then the existing bound is rechecked again. Persisted clocks never restore tenure. Cleanup is administrative, not program execution. |\n| 7. Reopen | Fresh receiver reconstruction uses canonical recovery, not original machine. Occurrence, waits, retained ids, descriptors and byte identity survive. Incomplete preparations stay non-runnable: no invented waits, successor remint or blind uncertain-serving retry. |\n| 8. Uncertain append | Step, abort, enroll and hand-off refuse progression while stalled. Reads distinguish authenticated blocked tail from transport failure, gaps/stagnation and malformed frames. Only reopen reconciles uncertainty. |\n| 9. Holder recovery | Durable grant restores no executing machine. Matching release precedes candidacy. Newer grants outrank old exits; old release acknowledgments cannot discharge another lease. D13 candidate/admitted-variant checks retained. |\n| 10. C12 enrollment | Persist derived identity/outcome; reconcile authenticated enrollment before retry. Unavailable evidence waits without another call. Reopen retains enrollment progress even without a complete source snapshot. |\n| 11. Run end / residual 2 | Ended gate, stopped IO, one diagnostic, cleanup release and no successor retained. Divergence changes the actual cursor-resolved input identity. Conflict is generated after activation. Ordinary failed occurrence regrants through the judge; conflict stays quarantined/ungrantable. |\n\nSource crash coverage includes **22 before/after-visibility cuts** over mint, serving, dual storage, fence and offer. Exit coverage enumerates every dynamically produced journal boundary with both cut modes, plus report/release/closure recovery. Other rows cover successful retry with uncertain attempt append, proposal send/carriage recovery, pre-attachment grant durability and enrollment reconciliation.\n\nRestarted exits do not resend uncommitted reports using saved tenure. They retain exit obligations while carrying cleanup release and reconciling history. If the original queued report commits during cleanup, its exact closure and successor offer still complete; otherwise they re-enter candidacy from the origin checkpoint. This conservative interpretation is explicit and tested, including delayed original report carriage after restart.\n\n## Exact final tests and checks\n\n| Gate | Outcome | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.ucf.holder.driver-test` | **66 tests, 1026 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors; exit 0** | `/private/tmp/d14-final-driver3.log` |\n| `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.ucf.holder.export-test -n yin.vm.ucf.handoff-test -n yin.vm.ucf.handoff-v1-test` | **69 tests, 702 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors; exit 0** | `/private/tmp/d14-final-seam.log` |\n| `bb test:clj` | **3556 tests, 235377 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors; exit 0** | `/private/tmp/d14-ruling-full-jvm-final5.log` |\n| `clojure -M:kondo --lint` on three source/two test files | **0 errors, 0 warnings; exit 0** | `/private/tmp/d14-final-kondo6.log` |\n| `cljstyle check` on those five files | **5 files checked, no incorrect formatting; exit 0** | `/private/tmp/d14-final-style4.log` and captured status |\n| `git diff --check` | **exit 0** | Final read-only check |\n\nFull lane completed Node REPL compilation (**184 files, 1 compiled, 0 warnings**) and pinned ANTLR generation. Fast-lane exclusions apply: slow tests excluded; five host-inapplicable CBOR cases print SKIP; Dart WS/REPL cross-host legs print SKIPPED because `build/ws-project-peer` and `build/yin-repl-peer` are absent. No dedicated Dart or Node driver suite ran.\n\nAn initial sandbox full run encountered socket/transport restrictions and was interrupted. Four approved intermediate full runs were also interrupted during subsequent lint/legacy-dependency/report-carriage/renewal corrections. These exited 130 without aggregates and are not completed-suite evidence. The final approved run above completed against final code. Lint and formatting were not sandbox-blocked.\n\n## Red and green evidence\n\nInherited baseline: **48 driver tests / 490 assertions / 24 failures / 1 error** (`/private/tmp/d14-baseline.log`). Earlier audit full lane: **3529 tests / 234739 assertions / 25 failures / 1 error** (`/private/tmp/d14-full-fast-escalated.log`). Its additional store-write audit failure came from the composition byte-store slot; renaming it internally to `:content-store` resolves that failure without changing the allowlist.\n\nActual regression cycles, in tests/assertions/failures/errors order:\n\n| Red behavior | Red outcome | Green evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Missing recovery APIs | 16 / 86 / 6 / 0 | Initial seam 16 / 98 / 0 / 0, then independent gate |\n| Validation before attachment | 17 / 110 / 3 / 0 | 17 / 110 / 0 / 0 |\n| Alias/cell byte reproduction | 18 / 124 / 5 / 2 | 18 / 124 / 0 / 0 |\n| Storage write-ahead brackets | 55 / 524 / 7 / 0 | 56 / 531 / 0 / 0 |\n| Grant durable before lower | 64 / 1010 / 1 / 0 | 64 / 1010 / 0 / 0 |\n| Receiver contamination | 21 / 140 / 4 / 0 | 21 / 140 / 0 / 0 |\n| Real retained FFI route | 24 / 166 / 3 / 0 | 24 / 166 / 0 / 0 |\n| Complete legacy dependencies | 24 / 168 / 4 / 0 | 24 / 168 / 0 / 0 |\n| Snapshot/body binding before attachment | 24 / 174 / 2 / 0 | Final independent seam gate |\n| Stalled public hand-off | 1 / 3 / 1 / 0 | Final driver gate |\n| Delayed original report carriage | 1 / 9 / 3 / 0 | 65 / 1020 / 0 / 0, then final driver |\n| Renewal acknowledgment/bound recheck | 2 / 29 / 5 / 0 | Final driver 66 / 1026 / 0 / 0 |\n\nRed logs: `/private/tmp/d14-seam-red.log`, `/private/tmp/d14-validation-red.log`, `/private/tmp/d14-seam-alias.log`, `/private/tmp/d14-storage-brackets-red.log`, `/private/tmp/d14-grant-durability-red.log`, `/private/tmp/d14-fresh-state-red.log`, `/private/tmp/d14-ffi-route-red.log`, `/private/tmp/d14-legacy-complete-red.log`, `/private/tmp/d14-snapshot-counter-red.log`, `/private/tmp/d14-stalled-handoff-red2.log`, `/private/tmp/d14-delayed-report-red.log`, `/private/tmp/d14-renewal-brackets-red2.log`.\n\nSome preparatory commands failed compilation or used an unsupported test-selection flag; some initial fixtures did not exercise the intended pending variant. They are not claimed as successful tests or meaningful red behavior. The FFI fixture was corrected to a genuinely blocked request before its red/green cycle. No claim is made that every exploratory edit had a separate red run; the table records actual evidence.\n\n## Remaining concerns / incomplete work\n\nNo known requested implementation row remains incomplete on JVM evidence. Architect/reviewer validation is still required, particularly for the recovery format and conservative uncommitted-report restart interpretation. Dedicated Node/Dart lanes, missing Dart peers, slow lanes and production backend fault testing were not run and are not claimed. Incomplete snapshots and unavailable/corrupt history deliberately fail closed, not automatically repair or authorize execution.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
